{"role":"assistant","content":"Let me try fetching ScienceDirect data via webfetch and also try to read the xlsx files with Python.","toolCalls":[{"id":"call_1855a2906f1c4e3c90362e6a","name":"webfetch","arguments":{"prompt":"Find all Life Sciences domains listed under Reference Works and the number of journals or publications in each domain. Also find the count for Health Sciences. Look for any tables or lists showing the number of Reference Works per subject domain.","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/medicine-and-dentistry/reference-works"}},{"id":"call_35a46ff51fc64d888900a259","name":"webfetch","arguments":{"prompt":"List all subject areas and their Reference Works counts. Find data about Life Sciences domains and Health Sciences Reference Works numbers.","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/subjects"}},{"id":"call_b74114c45df544b7b00e4d23","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /d D:\\GoatCode-ts\\gaia && python -c \"\nimport openpyxl\nimport os\n\ndata_dir = 'data'\nfor f in os.listdir(data_dir):\n    if f.endswith('.xlsx'):\n        path = os.path.join(data_dir, f)\n        try:\n            wb = openpyxl.load_workbook(path, data_only=True)\n            for sheet_name in wb.sheetnames:\n                ws = wb[sheet_name]\n                # Print first few rows to understand structure\n                rows = list(ws.iter_rows(values_only=True))\n                if rows:\n                    print(f'=== {f} -> {sheet_name} (first 5 rows) ===')\n                    for row in rows[:5]:\n                        print(row)\n                    print()\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f'{f}: {e}')\n\"\n"}}]}
