B) \\u2194 (\\u00acB \\u2192 \\u00acA)\\n(A \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (\\u00acA \\u2228 B)\\n(\\u00acA \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (A \\u2228 \\u00acB)\\n\\u00ac(A \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (A \\u2227 \\u00acB)\\n\\nWhich of the above is not logically equivalent to the rest? Provide the full s\",\r\n   37\t  \"gold\": \"(\\u00acA \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (A \\u2228 \\u00acB)\",\r\n   38\t  \"got\": \"(\\u00acA \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (A \\u2228 \\u00acB)\",\r\n   39\t  \"secs\": 10.5,\r\n   40\t  \"raw_tail\": \"3, 4, and 6 are all valid logical equivalences (tautologies).\\nStatement 5, $(\\\\neg A \\\\rightarrow B) \\\\leftrightarrow (A \\\\lor \\\\neg B)$, is NOT a logical equivalence (it is invalid/contingent).\\n\\nThe question asks for the full statement that doesn't fit:\\n(\\u00acA \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (A \\u2228 \\u00acB)\\n\\nANSWER: (\\u00acA \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (A \\u2228 \\u00acB)\\n\\n\"\r\n   41\t },\r\n   42\t {\r\n   43\t  \"task_id\": \"2d83110e-a098-4ebb-9987-066c06fa42d0\",\r\n   44\t  \"level\": 1,\r\n   45\t  \"file\": false,\r\n   46\t  \"question\": \".rewsna eht sa \\\"tfel\\\" drow eht fo etisoppo eht etirw ,ecnetnes siht dnatsrednu uoy fI\",\r\n   47\t  \"gold\": \"Right\",\r\n   48\t  \"got\": \"right\",\r\n   49\t  \"secs\": 12.5,\r\n   50\t  \"raw_tail\": \" user's question is written in reverse text:\\n\\\".rewsna eht sa \\\"tfel\\\" drow eht fo etisoppo eht etirw ,ecnetnes siht dnatsrednu uoy fI\\\"\\n\\nReversed:\\n\\\"If you understand this sentence, write the opposite of the word \\\"left\\\" as the answer.\\\"\\n\\nThe opposite of \\\"left\\\" is \\\"right\\\".\\n\\nANSWER: right\\n\\n\\n[tool bash {}]\\n\"\r\n   51\t },\r\n   52\t {\r\n   53\t  \"task_id\": \"305ac316-eef6-4446-960a-92d80d542f82\",\r\n   54\t  \"level\": 1,\r\n   55\t  \"file\": false,\r\n   56\t  \"question\": \"Who did the actor who played Ray in the Polish-language version of Everybody Loves Raymond play in Magda M.? Give only the first name.\",\r\n   57\t  \"gold\": \"Wojciech\",\r\n   58\t  \"got\": \"Wojciech\",\r\n   59\t  \"secs\": 15.8,\r\n   60\t  \"raw_tail\": \"ANSWER: Wojciech\\n\\n\"\r\n   61\t },\r\n   62\t {\r\n   63\t  \"task_id\": \"389793a7-ca17-4e82-81cb-2b3a2391b4b9\",\r\n   64\t  \"level\": 1,\r\n   65\t  \"file\": true,\r\n   66\t  \"question\": \"You are a telecommunications engineer who wants to build cell phone towers on a stretch of road. In the reference file is a layout of the road and nearby houses. Each dash, \\\"-\\\", is a marker indicating\",\r\n   67\t  \"gold\": \"3\",\r\n   68\t  \"got\": \"3\",\r\n   69\t  \"secs\": 74.8,\r\n   70\t  \"raw_tail\": \"tool read {}]\\n\\n[tool read {}]\\n\\n[tool read {}]\\n\\n[tool read {\\\"path\\\":\\\"data/389793a7-ca17-4e82-81cb-2b3a2391b4b9.txt\\\"}]\\n\\n[tool read {\\\"path\\\":\\\"data/389793a7-ca17-4e82-81cb-2b3a2391b4b9.txt\\\"}]\\n\\n[tool bash {\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -c \\\\\\\"with open('data/389793a7-ca17-4e82-81cb-2b3a2391b4b9.txt', 'r') as f: print(]\\n\"\r\n   71\t },\r\n   72\t {\r\n   73\t  \"task_id\": \"3cef3a44-215e-4aed-8e3b-b1e3f08063b7\",\r\n   74\t  \"level\": 1,\r\n   75\t  \"file\": false,\r\n   76\t  \"question\": \"I'm making a grocery list for my mom, but she's a professor of botany and she's a real stickler when it comes to categorizing things. I need to add different foods to different categories on the groce\",\r\n   77\t  \"gold\": \"broccoli, celery, fresh basil, lettuce, sweet potatoes\",\r\n   78\t  \"got\": \"Broccoli, celery, sweet potatoes\",\r\n   79\t  \"secs\": 16.1,\r\n   80\t  \"raw_tail\": \"Broccoli, celery, sweet potatoes\\n\\n\"\r\n   81\t },\r\n   82\t {\r\n   83\t  \"task_id\": \"3f57289b-8c60-48be-bd80-01f8099ca449\",\r\n   84\t  \"level\": 1,\r\n   85\t  \"file\": false,\r\n   86\t  \"question\": \"How many at bats did the Yankee with the most walks in the 1977 regular season have that same season?\",\r\n   87\t  \"gold\": \"519\",\r\n   88\t  \"got\": \"525\",\r\n   89\t  \"secs\": 20.4,\r\n   90\t  \"raw_tail\": \"ANSWER: 525\\n\\n\"\r\n   91\t },\r\n   92\t {\r\n   93\t  \"task_id\": \"42576abe-0deb-4869-8c63-225c2d75a95a\",\r\n   94\t  \"level\": 1,\r\n   95\t  \"file\": false,\r\n   96\t  \"question\": \"In the fictional language of Tizin, basic sentences are arranged with the Verb first, followed by the direct object, followed by the subject of the sentence. I want to express my love for apples to my\",\r\n   97\t  \"gold\": \"Maktay mato apple\",\r\n   98\t  \"got\": \"Maktay Mato Apple\",\r\n   99\t  \"secs\": 15.4,\r\n  100\t  \"raw_tail\": \"e apples) is **Apple** (nominative form of \\\"apples\\\", because it's the subject of the sentence).\\n\\n3. **Putting it together in VOS order:**\\n   - **Verb:** Maktay\\n   - **Direct Object:** Mato\\n   - **Subject:** Apple\\n\\nLet's combine them: **Maktay Mato Apple**\\n\\nANSWER: Maktay Mato Apple\\n\\n\\n[tool todo {}]\\n\"\r\n... [1092 more lines]","toolCallId":"call_c304709f2ca543428e0418de","name":"read"}
