{"role":"tool","content":"    1\t[\r\n    2\t {\r\n    3\t  \"task_id\": \"0383a3ee-47a7-41a4-b493-519bdefe0488\",\r\n    4\t  \"question\": \"On the BBC Earth YouTube video of the Top 5 Silliest Animal Moments, what species of bird is featured?\",\r\n    5\t  \"gold\": \"Rockhopper penguin\",\r\n    6\t  \"got\": \"Penguin\",\r\n    7\t  \"secs\": 10.7,\r\n    8\t  \"raw_tail\": \"ANSWER: Penguin\\n\\n\",\r\n    9\t  \"correct\": false\r\n   10\t },\r\n   11\t {\r\n   12\t  \"task_id\": \"11af4e1a-5f45-467d-9aeb-46f4bb0bf034\",\r\n   13\t  \"question\": \"How many more blocks (also denoted as layers) in BERT base encoder than the encoder from the architecture proposed in Attention is All You Need?\",\r\n   14\t  \"gold\": \"6\",\r\n   15\t  \"got\": \"6\",\r\n   16\t  \"secs\": 11.1,\r\n   17\t  \"raw_tail\": \"To find how many more blocks (layers) the BERT-base encoder has compared to the encoder from the architecture proposed in *Attention Is All You Need*:\\n\\n* **BERT-base Encoder:** Has **12** encoder layers (transformer blocks).\\n* **Attention Is All You Need (Transformer) Encoder:** Has **6** encoder layers (stacked $N = 6$ times).\\n\\nCalculation: \\n$$12 - 6 = 6$$\\n\\nANSWER: 6\\n\\n\",\r\n   18\t  \"correct\": true\r\n   19\t },\r\n   20\t {\r\n   21\t  \"task_id\": \"23dd907f-1261-4488-b21c-e9185af91d5e\",\r\n   22\t  \"question\": \"In Audre Lorde\\u2019s poem \\u201cFather Son and Holy Ghost\\u201d, what is the number of the stanza in which some lines are indented?\",\r\n   23\t  \"gold\": \"2\",\r\n   24\t  \"got\": \"2\",\r\n   25\t  \"secs\": 14.0,\r\n   26\t  \"raw_tail\": \"ANSWER: 2\\n\\n\",\r\n   27\t  \"correct\": true\r\n   28\t },\r\n   29\t {\r\n   30\t  \"task_id\": \"27d5d136-8563-469e-92bf-fd103c28b57c\",\r\n   31\t  \"question\": \"\\u00ac(A \\u2227 B) \\u2194 (\\u00acA \\u2228 \\u00acB)\\n\\u00ac(A \\u2228 B) \\u2194 (\\u00acA \\u2227 \\u00acB)\\n(A \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (\\u00acB \\u2192 \\u00acA)\\n(A \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (\\u00acA \\u2228 B)\\n(\\u00acA \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (A \\u2228 \\u00acB)\\n\\u00ac(A \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (A \\u2227 \\u00acB)\\n\\nWhich of the above is not logically eq\",\r\n   32\t  \"gold\": \"(\\u00acA \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (A \\u2228 \\u00acB)\",\r\n   33\t  \"got\": \"(\\u00acA \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (A \\u2228 \\u00acB)\",\r\n   34\t  \"secs\": 10.1,\r\n   35\t  \"raw_tail\": \"B)$**\\n   - The negation of an implication is $\\\\neg(A \\\\to B) \\\\equiv \\\\neg(\\\\neg A \\\\vee B) \\\\equiv A \\\\wedge \\\\neg B$. \\n   - Therefore, this biconditional statement is a **tautology** (always true).\\n\\nThus, the statement $(\\\\neg A \\\\to B) \\\\leftrightarrow (A \\\\\\u2228 \\\\neg B)$ is the only one that is not logically equivalent to a tautology (i.e., not logically equivalent to the rest).\\n\\nANSWER: (\\u00acA \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (A \\u2228 \\u00acB)\\n\\n\",\r\n   36\t  \"correct\": true\r\n   37\t },\r\n   38\t {\r\n   39\t  \"task_id\": \"2d83110e-a098-4ebb-9987-066c06fa42d0\",\r\n   40\t  \"question\": \".rewsna eht sa \\\"tfel\\\" drow eht fo etisoppo eht etirw ,ecnetnes siht dnatsrednu uoy fI\",\r\n   41\t  \"gold\": \"Right\",\r\n   42\t  \"got\": \"Right\",\r\n   43\t  \"secs\": 11.6,\r\n   44\t  \"raw_tail\": \"ANSWER: Right\\n\\n\\n[tool websearch {}]\\n\",\r\n   45\t  \"correct\": true\r\n   46\t },\r\n   47\t {\r\n   48\t  \"task_id\": \"305ac316-eef6-4446-960a-92d80d542f82\",\r\n   49\t  \"question\": \"Who did the actor who played Ray in the Polish-language version of Everybody Loves Raymond play in Magda M.? Give only the first name.\",\r\n   50\t  \"gold\": \"Wojciech\",\r\n... [330 more lines]","toolCallId":"call_ae4ec13256954088a494ab80","name":"read"}
